# Cursor Rules — Mileway IT Capacity Planner

These rules apply to all code written in this repository. They encode hard decisions made during
the design and implementation of the VS Finance capacity planning tool. Follow them exactly.

---

## 1. DUAL-TRACK IT/BIZ ASSIGNEES — NON-NEGOTIABLE

Every level of the Jira hierarchy (Epic, Feature, Story, Phase) must support BOTH an IT assignee
and a BIZ assignee. Never add assignee fields that cover only one track.

- IT track = TeamMember, primary colour `#0ED3CF` (teal / `sana-teal`)
- BIZ track = BusinessContact, colour `#7C3AED` (purple / `biz.DEFAULT`)
- The slide-out panel ALWAYS shows both in a two-column grid (IT | Business)
- If a new component involves assigning people, it must have both tracks or neither

---

## 2. NO TEXT LABELS ON GANTT BARS

Gantt bars are plain coloured rectangles. They do NOT contain text, percentages, names, or icons
inside the bar rectangle. Assignees and details are only visible in the slide-out panel.

Avatar stacks INSIDE bars are also not currently implemented and should not be added without an
explicit decision to do so.

---

## 3. SPRINT FRACTION SYSTEM — USE DATES, NOT FRACTIONS

The sprint fraction formula is a conceptual model for documentation only.
In the runtime implementation, bar positions are computed from ISO dates, not stored fractions.

- `sprint_start` and `sprint_end` are NOT stored on JiraWorkItem — do not add these fields
- Bar `left` and `width` are calculated from `(date - viewStart) / (viewEnd - viewStart)`
- Do not add new position calculation approaches; use the existing `barLayout()` function

---

## 4. QUARTER-FIRST DESIGN

The default time granularity is a SINGLE QUARTER (6 sprints). Full-year is always a secondary
toggle. When designing a new view:

- Default to single-quarter display
- Implement full-year as a toggle, not the default
- Sprint columns default to 6 equal columns filling the available width
- Quarter navigation (prev/next) is always present in quarter mode

---

## 5. DESIGN LANGUAGE — "EDITORIAL CALM"

The UI follows a warm editorial aesthetic (Sana Labs style): warm off-white backgrounds,
serif headings, teal/orange accents. No Mileway navy, no blue primary.

- Page background: `sana-bg` (`#FAF9F7`) — warm off-white
- Card surface: `sana-bg-card` (`#FFFFFF`) — pure white
- Primary accent: `sana-teal` (`#0ED3CF`) — teal
- Secondary accent: `sana-orange` (`#F97316`) — orange
- No decorative gradients
- No shadows on Gantt bars — shadows only on elevated/floating elements (modals, dropdowns, tooltips)
- Shadows use the defined scale: `shadow-sm`, `shadow-md`, `shadow-lg`, `shadow-xl` from Tailwind config

---

## 6. NEVER SET overflow: hidden ON GANTT ROWS

The gantt continuation arrows (.gantt-bar-clip-left::before, .gantt-bar-clip-right::after) are
CSS pseudo-elements that render OUTSIDE the bar's own bounding box. If any ancestor gantt row
gets overflow: hidden, these arrows will be silently clipped and disappear.

This rule applies to:
- The gantt row div (the div containing the bar, with the height: h style)
- Any wrapper around multiple rows
- Do NOT add overflow: hidden to gantt containers

The gantt area outer container CAN use overflow-x: auto for horizontal scrolling.

---

## 7. DESIGN TOKENS — SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH

### `frontend/src/theme/tokens.ts` is the JS-side source of truth.

All JS/TSX colour usage (Gantt bars, heatmap cells, chart series, inline styles) must reference
named exports from `tokens.ts`:

- `Background.*` — page and surface backgrounds
- `Text.*` — primary / secondary / tertiary / inverse text
- `Accent.*` — teal, orange, coral, magenta, green, red
- `Border.*` — subtle / light border colours
- `Biz.*` — BIZ track purple palette
- `Semantic.*` — success / warning / danger colours + their bg/border variants
- `GanttBar.*` — Gantt bar colours by item type (SEMANTIC — do not restyle)
- `HeatmapTiers.*` — heatmap cell tier colours (SEMANTIC — do not restyle)
- `ChartColors.*` — chart series colours
- `Shadow.*` — box-shadow strings
- `Radius.*` — border-radius values
- `Duration.*` — animation duration values (ms)

**Never hardcode a hex value in a component or screen file.** Use `tokens.ts` exports for
inline styles; use Tailwind token names (`sana-teal`, `util-healthy`, `biz`, etc.) for
class-based styling.

### Tailwind colour namespace:

| Namespace | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `sana.*` | Primary design system tokens (backgrounds, text, accents, borders) |
| `util.*` | Semantic capacity status colours (bench / healthy / near / over) |
| `biz.*` | BIZ track purple palette |
| `mw.*` | **Legacy aliases only** — kept so old `mw-*` class names compile. Do NOT use in new code. |

If you need a new colour, add it to both `tokens.ts` AND `tailwind.config.js`. Never add to one without the other.

---

## 8. TYPOGRAPHY

Two fonts are in use — never add a third without an explicit decision:

- **Body / UI text:** `DM Sans` — loaded from Google Fonts in `index.html`. Applied via
  Tailwind's default `font-sans`. Weights 400, 500, 600.
- **Page titles / editorial headings:** `Source Serif 4` — loaded from Google Fonts.
  Applied via `font-heading` Tailwind class OR inline `style={{ fontFamily: "'Source Serif 4', Georgia, serif" }}`.
  Use `font-heading` for editorial headings only; use `font-sans` for everything else.

Minimum text size: `text-xs` (11px). Do not use text smaller than 11px anywhere in the UI.

Font scale (defined in `tailwind.config.js`):

| Token | Size |
|---|---|
| `text-xs` | 11px |
| `text-sm` | 13px |
| `text-base` / `text-md` | 15px |
| `text-lg` | 16px |
| `text-xl` | 18px |
| `text-2xl` | 24px |
| `text-3xl` | 32px |
| `text-4xl` | 40px |

---

## 9. LAYOUT — SIDEBAR + CONTENT (NO HEADER)

The app uses a **flex-row sidebar-beside-content** layout. `Header.tsx` is retired (file exists
but is not imported). Do not re-introduce a horizontal top navigation.

`Layout.tsx` structure:
```
<div className="flex h-screen overflow-hidden bg-[#FAF9F7]">
  <Sidebar />
  <div className="flex flex-col flex-1 min-w-0 overflow-hidden">
    <NotificationBanners />
    <main className="flex-1 overflow-auto px-10 py-8 max-w-[1440px] w-full mx-auto">
      {children}
    </main>
  </div>
</div>
```

### Sidebar rules:

- Expanded: `w-[240px]`, Collapsed: `w-[60px]`
- Collapse state persisted to `localStorage` key `ui.sidebarCollapsed`
- Width transition: `transition-[width] duration-standard ease-in-out` (250ms)
- Background: `sana-bg` (`#FAF9F7`) with `border-r border-sana-border` — light/warm, NOT navy
- Active nav item: `border-l-[3px] border-[#0ED3CF] bg-sana-bg-highlight text-sana-text font-semibold`
- Inactive nav item: `border-l-[3px] border-transparent text-sana-text-muted hover:text-sana-text hover:bg-sana-bg-secondary`
- Collapsed mode: show icon only, hide all text labels

### NotificationBanners:

- Sits between sidebar and main content as a zero-height-when-empty strip
- Contains: Jira baseline warning (orange/amber) + active scenario banner (teal)
- Do NOT move these into page components

---

## 10. PAGE HEADER PATTERN

All pages use `<PageHeader>` from `components/layout/PageHeader.tsx`. Do not create custom
page title/subtitle markup inline — always use the shared component.

- Title: `text-4xl font-bold` Source Serif 4, `#1A1A1A`, `letter-spacing: -0.02em`
- Subtitle: `text-base` DM Sans, `#6B7280` (muted)
- Optional `actions` prop: right-aligned, vertically centered with title

---

## 11. CARDS & SURFACES

- Card border-radius: `rounded-card` (16px)
- Card background: `bg-white` (`sana-bg-card`)
- Card border: `border border-sana-border` (`#E5E5E3`)
- Do NOT add left accent borders to all cards — accent borders are used selectively for highlight
  panels or navigation active states only
- Page background: `bg-sana-bg` (`#FAF9F7`)
- Shadows: only on elevated/floating elements — `shadow-sm` for tooltips, `shadow-md` for dropdowns,
  `shadow-lg` for modals. Never on flat cards in the page flow.

---

## 12. STATUS BADGES — USE `Badge.tsx`

All status indicators use the `Badge` component from `components/ui/Badge.tsx`.
Do NOT create custom inline status chips or spans.

Badge is pill-shaped (`rounded-full`) with ALL-CAPS (`uppercase`) text.
Available variants:

`default` | `success` / `green` | `warning` / `amber` | `danger` / `red` |
`primary` / `blue` | `outline` | `grey` | `tentative` |
`beginner` | `intermediate` | `advanced` | `expert`

Common mappings:
- Capacity healthy → `success`
- Capacity near → `warning`
- Capacity overloaded → `danger`
- IT track → `primary`
- BIZ track → use purple inline (no badge variant for BIZ — use `Biz.*` tokens directly)

---

## 13. CAPACITY THRESHOLDS — OVERLOADED DEFINITION

"Overloaded" = allocatedDays > availableDays in a sprint.

- Healthy = ≤ 90% utilisation → colour `util-healthy` (`#22C55E`, green)
- Warning = > 90% → colour `util-near` (`#F97316`, orange)
- Overloaded = > 100% → colour `util-over` (`#EF4444`, red)

This is a hard threshold at 100%. Do NOT use a configurable threshold for the overloaded state.
This definition must be consistent across ALL views that show capacity (Gantt, heatmap, dashboard cards).

---

## 14. BAR POSITIONING USES PERCENTAGE-BASED left/width — NOT CSS GRID COLUMNS

Gantt bars use `position: absolute` with:
- `left: ${(barLayout.left * 100).toFixed(2)}%`
- `width: ${(barLayout.width * 100).toFixed(2)}%`

The column grid (CSS `grid-template-columns: repeat(N, 1fr)`) is ONLY used for the time header
row and the vertical grid lines. It is NEVER used to position bars.

---

## 15. SLIDE-OUT PANEL IS THE SINGLE DETAIL VIEW

For all item types (JiraWorkItem, LocalPhase, TeamMember detail), the slide-out panel is the
canonical detail surface. Do NOT:

- Create inline edit forms that expand inside the table/gantt
- Create a second modal form that duplicates the panel content
- Add editable fields directly on row items (except the small BIZ days input on the Epics tree)

The panel slides in from the right (420px wide), has a backdrop overlay, and closes on Escape.

---

## 16. CHARTS — RECHARTS STYLING

All recharts charts must follow this style:

- **No `<CartesianGrid />`** on any chart
- Y-axis: `tickCount={3}`, `axisLine={false}`, `tickLine={false}`, tick `fill: Text.tertiary` (`#9CA3AF`), `fontFamily: 'DM Sans'`
- X-axis: `axisLine={false}`, `tickLine={false}`, same tick style
- Bar radius: `[4, 4, 0, 0]`
- Tooltip: use `<ChartTooltip />` from `components/ui/ChartTooltip.tsx` — never the default recharts tooltip
- Series colours: use `ChartColors.*` from `tokens.ts` (primary=orange, secondary=magenta, tertiary=teal)

---

## 17. DARK MODE — DEFERRED

Dark mode is architecturally wired (`darkMode: 'class'` in Tailwind) but **not implemented**.

- `DarkSurface` in `tokens.ts` is `{}` and `@deprecated`
- The `mw.*` dark surface stubs are no-ops (same as light values)
- Do NOT add new `dark:` Tailwind variant classes to components
- Do NOT implement dark mode styling for new components until a decision is made to un-defer it
- The dark mode toggle in the sidebar UI can remain but has no visual effect

---

## 18. HIERARCHY STRUCTURE — NEVER SKIP LEVELS

The hierarchy is ALWAYS: Epic → Feature → Story | Phase

- A Story cannot be the direct child of an Epic (must go through Feature)
- A LocalPhase (UAT/Hypercare) is attached to an Epic, NOT to a Feature
- Do not create new hierarchy levels between or below the existing ones without an explicit design decision

---

## 19. TECH STACK — NO NEW DEPENDENCIES WITHOUT REVIEW

The frontend uses: React 19, TypeScript, Vite, Tailwind CSS, Zustand, Supabase JS SDK,
lucide-react (icons), date-fns, clsx, xlsx, recharts.

Do not add new dependencies for things already covered by the existing stack:
- No new icon libraries (use lucide-react)
- No new CSS-in-JS (use Tailwind)
- No new state management (use Zustand)
- No new UI component libraries (use the existing `ui/` components)
- No new charting libraries (use recharts)
- No new font packages — DM Sans and Source Serif 4 are loaded from Google Fonts in `index.html`

---

## 20. SUPABASE MIGRATIONS

Database changes MUST be expressed as new numbered migration files in `supabase/migrations/`.
Do NOT edit `schema.sql` directly. Migration files are numbered sequentially (e.g. `027_...`).

---

## 21. TypeScript TYPES IN types/index.ts

All new TypeScript interfaces and types belong in `frontend/src/types/index.ts`.
Do NOT scatter type definitions across component files. Inline type definitions are only
acceptable for component-local state types (e.g. `type TabType = 'it' | 'biz' | 'all'`).

---

## 22. DOCS STAY IN SYNC — UPDATE ON EVERY COMMIT

⚠️ THIS IS A HARD RULE. Do not end any coding session without completing it.

After every session that changes code, you MUST update documentation BEFORE the final commit.

Trigger → what to update:
- New or changed data entity (`types/index.ts`)   → `docs/data-model.md`
- New or changed component / page               → `docs/views/<view>.md` or `docs/architecture.md`
- New feature or view status change             → `docs/README.md` (views table)
- Architectural change (store, sync, routing)   → `docs/architecture.md`
- Any code change at all                        → `docs/CHANGELOG.md` (add entry at top)

CHANGELOG entry format:
  ## [YYYY-MM-DD] — <short title>
  ### Added / Changed / Fixed
  - one bullet per meaningful change
  ### Docs updated
  - list each doc file touched and what was updated

CHECKLIST — before every commit, confirm:
  [ ] docs/CHANGELOG.md has a new entry at the top for today's date
  [ ] All other affected docs listed above are updated
  [ ] The doc updates are staged in the same commit as the code

Never commit code without a matching CHANGELOG.md entry.
The CHANGELOG.md entry must be committed in the same commit as the code change.
